            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Other ideas?\n\nI think we should support then `typing.NoReturn` and `typing.Never` [1]. Although they can have also slightly different meaning like \"This function should be never called\", but at least mypy [2] threats them as function that only raises exception (and never returns)\n\n**EDIT**: Now I am rereading the issue and this issue is slightly about something else. `typing.NoReturn` means that function does not return back and this PR is about function that returns `void` or raises exceptions. In any case, it would be great to add `typing.NoReturn` too...\n\n[1] https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Never\n[2] https://mypy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/more_types.html#the-noreturn-type\n[3] https://typing.python.org/en/latest/spec/special-types.html#noreturn",
