            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Another idea. In python for function returning nothing to use `-> None`. Cannot we optimize this kind of function instead?\n\n1. Now if function:\n   ```python\n   @cfunc\n   def bar() -> None\n       return 5\n   ```\n   does not return compilation error. This can be change to a compilation error. (Not sure how breaking change this can be for users though)\n2. Function `bar()` then can be optimized as mentioned in issue description. If user does `foo = bar()` we can just assign `Py_None` to C variable representing `foo` variable.",
